-- Q11641: Accounting Changes and Error Corrections [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): ASC 250-10-45-5 requires the cumulative effect of a change in accounting principle to be reflected by adjusting the opening balance of retained earnings for the earliest period presented. Unlike the former cumulative-effect method eliminated by SFAS 154, the adjustment never flows through current income.
Wrong (B): The cumulative effect is not recognized on the current-year income statement; that approach was superseded by ASC 250 (SFAS 154).
Wrong (C): Other comprehensive income is used for items like unrealized gains and foreign currency adjustments, not accounting principle changes.
Wrong (D): The cumulative effect is an equity adjustment, not a deferred charge; it has no future economic benefit to recognize as an asset.$EXPL$
