  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): ASC 250-10-20 defines retrospective application as impracticable when the entity cannot determine period-specific effects after making every reasonable effort. This occurs when required historical data was not collected in prior periods, as with Waverly''s missing cost-layer data.
Wrong (A): An entity''s preference for prospective treatment does not satisfy the impracticability exception; retrospective application is mandatory unless genuinely impracticable.
Wrong (B): The direction of the earnings impact is irrelevant to impracticability; the test is whether effects can be determined, not whether they are favorable.
Wrong (C): Auditor approval is not a criterion under ASC 250; impracticability is assessed based on the entity''s ability to determine prior-period effects.$EXPL$
